#. type: Title #
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Release Sync"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keeps `_data/releases.yaml` patch versions current by fetching from the GitHub API,\n"
"and upcoming releases current by reading the\n"
"[Release Planning wiki](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Release-Planning).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:7
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "What it does"
msgstr "O que ele faz"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fetches releases from GitHub API\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups by minor version (3.36.x becomes \"3.36\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Updates `latest_patch` and `latest_patch_date` for each minor\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reads the Release Planning wiki (raw markdown) and replaces the upcoming entries with every\n"
"release whose Platform release date is today or later (including `(Proposal)` entries)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preserves all manually-edited fields\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upcoming releases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Upcoming releases come from the wiki (`WikiReleasePlanning.java`). Each `## <major>.<minor> [LTS] [(Proposal)]`\n"
"heading with a \"Full Platform release ... on <date>\" bullet becomes an entry with `upcoming: true`,\n"
"`planned_date` set to that Platform date, `lts` set from the heading, and `proposal: true` if the heading is marked `(Proposal)`. Other headings\n"
"(e.g. `4.0 Beta1`) are ignored.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Existing `upcoming: true` entries are replaced by the wiki's entry for the same version, but\n"
"kept when the wiki has no usable entry for them (e.g. its date couldn't be parsed; a warning is\n"
"logged). Delete such an entry by hand once it is no longer planned.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the wiki can't be read and there are no hand-edited upcoming entries, the next release is\n"
"predicted from GitHub milestones, pre-release tags, or by cadence (next minor).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Field ownership"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Automated (updated by this script):**\n"
"- `latest_patch` - Latest patch version\n"
"- `latest_patch_date` - Date of latest patch\n"
"- `release_date` - Date of first release in this minor (published releases only)\n"
"- `rhbq.release_date`, `ibm.release_date` - When the minor first appeared in the Red Hat / IBM Maven repository (publish date of the earliest micro build of `quarkus-bom`, not an announced GA date). The provider block is created if the repository has the minor; its `eol_date` stays hand-edited. A date, once set, is never looked up or overwritten, so routine runs make no requests to these servers (the IBM one is rate limited). When a lookup is needed it uses Quarkus REST Client interfaces (`MavenRepositories`) with SmallRye Fault Tolerance: requests are sequential and paced, transient failures (429, 5xx, I/O errors) are retried twice with exponential backoff, and a circuit breaker then stops all further requests to that server for the run; the gaps are filled by a later run. An enterprise `release_date` earlier than the community one is impossible: a scraped one is ignored with a warning, and the run fails before writing if any (including hand-edited) date is inconsistent\n"
"- `planned_date` - For upcoming releases: the planned Platform release date from the wiki\n"
"- `upcoming` - Set for releases listed as upcoming in the wiki; removed once the release is published\n"
"- `lts` - For upcoming releases only, taken from the wiki heading\n"
"- `proposal` - `true` for upcoming releases marked `(Proposal)` in the wiki\n"
"- `branched_from` - For published 3.x+ LTS releases that don't have one: the non-LTS minor (of the three below it) whose\n"
"  branch has the most recent merge-base with the LTS branch (`BranchLineage.java`). Release order and `main` aren't used: LTS\n"
"  policy changed over time (n-1 as parent, then concurrent n LTS / n+1 non-LTS releases) and `main` stopped being the trunk\n"
"  from 3.38. If candidates tie the newest is used, with a warning; if there are none the field stays blank (as for 2.x).\n"
"  Hand-edited values are never overwritten.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: tools/releases-sync/README.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Manual (edit directly in releases.yaml):**\n"
"- `policy` section - LTS cadence, support durations, descriptions\n"
"- `support_providers` section - Commercial support providers\n"
"- `eol_support` section - EOL support options\n"
"- `lts` - Whether this is an LTS release (published releases)\n"
"- `eol_date` - End of life date\n"
"- `link` - Blog post link\n"
"- `rhbq`, `ibm`, `herodevs` - Per-provider blocks; `eol_date` is hand-edited (herodevs `eol_date` can be a date or string like \"nes\")\n"
"- `upcoming`, `planned_date` - Only needed as a fallback when the wiki lists nothing usable for a release (`release_date` is only for published releases)\n"
msgstr ""

